===== pollux_phi_intro_plan.md =====
# pollux_phi — intro & plan
Hi swarm, I am **pollux_phi**. Senior DS, focused on medical image segmentation.
## Facts I confirmed (EDA)
- `data/train.csv`: 95,088 rows = 31,696 slices x 3 classes (`large_bowel`, `small_bowel`, `stomach`), RLE masks.
- `data/test.csv`: 20,400 rows = 6,800 slices x 3 classes; **test images are present** in `data/test/<case>/<day>/scans/*.png` (426 MB). So this is offline inference, not hidden test images.
- Non-empty fraction per class: large_bowel 0.366, small_bowel 0.288, stomach 0.225.
- 76 train cases, 28 test cases; **19 test cases also appear in train** (day/time split), 9 test cases are wholly unseen. → case-level holdout is the honest validation.
- Env: 1x A100 80GB (shared!), 128 CPUs, torch 2.2.0, timm 0.9.7, smp 0.3.4, albumentations 1.4.14. No MONAI.
- Metric = 0.4*Dice + 0.6*(1 - normalized 3D Hausdorff), mean over classes. Hausdorff matters a lot → postprocessing/outlier-slice removal is key.
## Proposed division of labour (please claim/comment)
1. **pollux_phi (me)**: 2.5D U-Net (smp, ImageNet encoder, 3 consecutive slices as channels), 3-class output, case-grouped val, full training + inference + RLE. Share weights and val scores.
2. Someone: metric implementation (dice-hausdorff per class, exactly as described) + submission validator — needed by everyone. Put in a shared message.
3. Someone: 3D/sequence approaches (e.g. 3D UNet or per-slice + 3D postproc) — different view.
4. Someone: strong 2D baseline with different backbone/resolution (e.g. effnet-b4 / convnext, 384px) to ensemble.
5. Someone: postprocessing research (remove isolated slices, fill holes, per-case smoothing, conform predictions to anatomy) evaluated on the shared holdout.
## Coordination rules I propose
- **Only ONE heavy GPU job at a time.** Announce in `blackboard` before launching; use `systemd-run --scope -p MemoryMax=...`. GPU ~40-60 GB max.
- Use a **common holdout split** so scores are comparable: hold out ~12 *entire cases* (including some days of partially-seen test cases). I will publish the exact case list in `[[pollux_phi_holdout_split.md]]`.
- Share OOF/holdout predictions as `.npy`/`.npz` in each workspace so we can ensemble.
I'm starting now with the data pipeline + holdout split + baseline. Will post scores with `<metric>..<\metric>` as soon as available. Ping me if you want to take a different task.
