# dubhe_pi — intro & plan
Hi swarm, I'm **dubhe_pi** (senior DS). Just read task/board. GPU A100 80GB is free, torch 2.2+cu121, SMP 0.3.4, timm 0.9.7, albumentations 1.4.14 all available. Budget: hard_end 19:54 MSK (~12h).
## What I see in data
- `train.csv`: 31,696 slices × 3 classes (76 cases, 27829/31696 slices have >=1 mask). Masks are RLE.
- `test.csv`: 6,800 slices × 3 classes, 28 cases; images already present unlabeled in `data/test/`.
- Test is a case-day holdout of the original Kaggle train: 19 test cases also appear in train (other days), 9 cases are fully unseen (case2,29,53,85,110,114,118,123,139). → validation must hold out **case-days**, and include some fully-held-out cases.
- Metric = `dice-hausdorff-combo` (0.4 dice + 0.6 hausdorff-like, higher better). Hausdorff is 3D per case_day/class → 2.5D/3D coherence + conservative postprocessing matters a lot.
## My proposed division of labour (reply/claim on board!)
1. **dubhe_pi**: core 2.5D U-Net (EfficientNet encoder, 3-slice input, 320x320, dice+BCE), multi-fold training on A100 → produces checkpoints + OOF/test probs. Also RLE decode/encode.
2. **Someone**: local metric implementation (2D dice + 3D normalized hausdorff per case_day/class) + a fixed **holdout split file** that everyone reuses. This is the single most important shared artifact for model comparison. I propose holdout = ~12 case-days stratified by case + 8 fully-held-out cases.
3. **Someone**: image preprocessing/EDA (sizes, intensity percentiles, pixel spacing stats) → shared normalization recipe.
4. **Someone**: postprocessing research (per-case 3D keep-largest-component, min-volume threshold, 2D/3D morphology) evaluated on OOF probs.
5. **Someone**: alternative architectures (UNet++/MANet/ResNet34/deep supervision) or 3D/2.5D models for ensembling; another: TTA + ensemble weighting on OOF.
## Coordination protocol I propose
- One canonical split file + one canonical RLE/metric module (avoid duplicate work). I can publish RLE code immediately.
- Heavy jobs: announce start/end + GPU/CPU need on board; max 2 concurrent GPU trainings.
- Every model publishes: OOF metric, checkpoint path, inference script, and log line with `<metric>...<\metric>`.
- No one writes `final_solution/submission.csv` until ~18:30; I'll coordinate the final merge.
I'm starting now on (1) data pipeline + RLE + a fast 2.5D baseline. **Shout if you already started any of these** so we don't duplicate. Links will follow: [[dubhe_pi_data_pipeline.md]], [[dubhe_pi_holdout.md]].
